# TODO
## Authentication & authorization

- [X] Authenticate submitters: invite → session token (`bbr_session_…`, SHA-256 in `user_sessions.token_hash`); only they can POST /user/messages
- [ ] Moderator/admin role: only they can approve, reject, list messages and see sender_ip (still a single static `ADMIN_TOKEN`)
- [X] Per-printer API tokens: SHA-256 hash in `printers.token_hash`, plain token returned once on create, `RequirePrinterToken` middleware puts the printer ID in the request context
- [X] Printer routes take the printer ID from the token instead of the URL (`/printer/heartbeat`, `/printer/messages/oldest/claim`)
- [X] Token rotation endpoint: `POST /admin/printers/{id}/rotate_token`
- [X] Printers can only update their own messages: processed/printed/failed scoped by `printer_id`; another printer's message returns 404, like an unknown ID
- [ ] Token revocation without issuing a new one (set `token_hash` to NULL, e.g. when retiring a printer)
- [X] Group routes in chi behind role-specific middleware (`/admin`, `/printer`, `/user`)
- [X] Decide which printers a submitter may target: `user_printers`, managed with `PUT /admin/users/{id}/printers`
- [X] Take sender_name from the logged-in identity, so people can't impersonate others (`sender_id` → `users.name`)
- [X] Admin routes for users: create with invite, reissue invite, list/revoke sessions
- [X] Write `user_sessions.last_used_at`: it exists in the schema and in the sessions response but is never set, so it is always `null`. Update it in `RequireUserToken` (or in `GetUserIDBySessionHash`), throttled to avoid a write on every request, e.g. `UPDATE user_sessions SET last_used_at = NOW() WHERE id = $1 AND (last_used_at IS NULL OR last_used_at < NOW() - INTERVAL '5 minutes')`. Useful to spot and revoke stale devices. Otherwise drop the column.
- [ ] Persistent session cookie (see `SCRATCHPAD.md`): `POST /users/claim` sets `__Host-bbr_session` (HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite=Lax, Max-Age 400 days) instead of returning the token in the body; `RequireUserToken` reads the bearer header, then the cookie; clear the cookie on 401; refresh it together with the throttled `last_used_at` update

## Printer ownership

- [X] `user_printers.role` (`member` / `owner`), with partial unique indexes: one owner per printer, one owned printer per user
- [X] Owner routes under `/user/printers/{id}` behind `RequirePrinterOwner`: quiet hours (set/clear), list/remove members, join tokens
- [X] Admin: `PUT /admin/users/{id}/printers` takes `printer_accesses` with roles
- [X] Map ownership constraint violations to 409 and unknown printers to 400 (`mapUserPrinterError`)
- [X] Removing a user's last printer revokes their sessions and clears their invite (`revokeAccessIfNoPrinters`, used by every removal path)
- [X] Removing a member rejects their `pending` / `awaiting_approval` messages to that printer
- [X] `SetPrinters` rejects queued messages for the printers it removes, like `RemoveMember` (shared `rejectQueuedMessages`)
- [X] Let users add their own devices: `POST /user/invite` returns a 15-minute invite for the caller (user ID from the session only); existing sessions are kept
- [X] Ownership transfer in one call: `PUT /admin/printers/{id}/owner {user_id}` (demotes the previous owner); `DELETE /admin/printers/{id}/owner?keep_as_member=` removes an owner without rewriting their other links. Replaces `PUT /admin/users/{id}/printers/{printerID}/owner`

## User lifecycle (join tokens)

- [X] Owners no longer create accounts (`POST /user/printers/{id}/members` removed): they hand out single-use, 2-day join tokens (`printer_join_tokens`). Owners never hold a credential for someone else's account
- [X] `POST /users/join` signs up a new account with a join token (401 if unusable); `POST /user/memberships` adds an existing account to the token's printer (400 if unusable, since the session is fine)
- [X] An owner's join token only works while they own the printer; losing ownership revokes their pending tokens (`revokeStaleJoinTokens`)
- [X] Names are unique per printer, case-insensitive (`ensureNameFreeOnPrinters`, under `lockPrinters`); not globally, to avoid name probing and squatting
- [X] Users list and revoke their own sessions (`GET /user/sessions` with `current`, `DELETE /user/sessions/{id}`), and leave a printer (`DELETE /user/memberships/{printerID}`, 409 for the owner)
- [X] Admin invite reissue is account recovery: revokes all sessions unless `{"revoke_sessions": false}`; 409 for a user with no printer
- [ ] Rate-limit the unauthenticated `POST /users/join` and `POST /users/claim` per IP (tokens are 130-bit, so this is about abuse, not guessing)
- [ ] Dormant accounts (no printer left) accumulate: an admin route to delete accounts, and an admin view of join tokens across printers
- [ ] Renaming accounts: must run the per-printer name check on all of the user's printers
- [ ] Add `httptest` tests for the users handlers (the lifecycle was checked end to end with curl against a seeded database)

